>  This is so true, like the outcomes of all wars.  Like all aggression,
>also, when one individual decides to exercise his aggressive propensity
>this imposes a responsibility on the other to defend: fight or perish.
>For my own part I am perfectly willing to discuss the grave issue that I
>have raised vigorously but entirely without rancor, and a mark of
>intelligence from the extropians would, in my view, suggest that they do
